{"name":"Jakarta Skyline","hex":"#3d325d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skyline","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The line that seems to be the boundary of the sky and the ground; the horizon.","The horizontal silhouette of a city or building against the sky."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To outline something against the sky.","To filter by means of the skyline operator."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skyline"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jakarta","blocks":[{"text":"Jakarta, officially the Special Capital Region of Jakarta, is the capital and largest city of Indonesia, with administrative status equivalent to a province. It lies on the northwestern coast of Java, bordering West Java and Banten and facing the Java Sea. Jakarta covers about 662 square kilometres and had 11 million registered residents in 2025. Its urban area extends well beyond the provincial boundary into the wider Jakarta metropolitan area, which had a population of nearly 42 million in 2025 according to the United Nations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Bundaran_Hotel_Indonesia_%282025%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bundaran_Hotel_Indonesia_%282025%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakarta","wikidata":"Q3630"},{"title":"Skyline","blocks":[{"text":"A skyline is the outline or shape viewed near the horizon. It can be created by a city's overall structure, or by human intervention in a rural setting, or in nature that is formed where the sky meets buildings or the land."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Lower_Manhattan_from_Governors_Island_with_a_fishing_boat_%2846294p%29.jpg/330px-Lower_Manhattan_from_Governors_Island_with_a_fishing_boat_%2846294p%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyline","wikidata":"Q465